    },
    {
      question: 'What materials and techniques are used for illuminated signs?',
      answer: 'Modern illuminated signs consist of: Housing made of powder-coated aluminum or stainless steel (rust-free, durable), front panels made of acrylic glass or polycarbonate (impact-resistant), LED modules as light source (energy-efficient, long-lasting). For 3D letters, we use aluminum profiles with LED backlighting or illuminated acrylic glass. All components are suitable for outdoor use (IP65).',
    },
    {
      question: 'How much electricity does an LED illuminated sign consume?',
      answer: 'LED illuminated signs are very energy efficient. A typical sign (approx. 2m wide) consumes only 50-150 watts. With 8 hours of daily operation, this equates to approximately CHF 50-150 in electricity costs per year (at 20 cents/kWh). Compared to neon tubes, you save up to 80% energy. Dimmable systems and timers reduce consumption further.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How long does an LED illuminated sign last?',
